---
title: Tofu & Broccoli on Rice
description: Crispy pan-fried tofu and boiled broccoli tossed in a glossy Chinese-style brown sauce, served over fluffy rice.
course: main
cuisine: Chinese
servings: 4
time required: 15 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Yo54RiBUx0&ab_channel=ProHomeCooks
image: https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/Pan-Fried-Sesame-Tofu-with-Broccoli-Close-1.jpg
tags:
  - tofu
  - stir fry
  - quick
  - rice bowl
---

Rinse @rice{2%cups} to remove the excess starch, then add it to a #pressure cooker{} along with the @water{2%cups}(plus 2 tbsp). Pressure cook for ~{4%minutes}.

Bring a #pot{} of water to a simmer on the stove. Set a #pan{} preheating on low heat and drizzle in some @oil{}.

Slice the @firm tofu{1%block} into 1/2 inch pieces, pat dry, and season with @salt and @pepper. Add to the preheated pan.

While the tofu fries, chop the @garlic{2%cloves} and @ginger{1%knob}, and cut the @broccoli{1%head} into florets. Flip the tofu to crisp up the second side.

In a bowl, whisk together the @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @Chinese cooking wine{2%tbsp}, @hoisin{2%tbsp}, @honey{1%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1%tbsp}, @chicken stock{0.25%cup}, and @cornstarch{1%tbsp} until there are no lumps.

Drop the broccoli into the simmering water and boil for ~{2%minutes}. Remove the tofu from the pan, then add the garlic and ginger and fry for ~{1-2%minutes}. Pour in the sauce and stir until it thickens and bubbles.

Cut up the tofu, then add it and the boiled broccoli into the pan. Stir to coat everything in the sauce and serve over the hot rice.
